    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/workplace-relations-specialist-other-nsw-australia-albury-wodonga-bathurst-dubbo-orange-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Workplace Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Workplace Relations Specialist - Other, NSW, Australia - Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Dubbo, NSW, Australia - Orange, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW Bathurst, NSW Dubbo, NSW Orange, NSW Other, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Show More Show Less Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 23 2026 Position Description Lead complex workplace relations matters across a multi-campus university Influence strategic people outcomes through trusted advice to senior leaders Enjoy 17% superannuation, flexible work options and generous leave benefits The role Full Time, Fixed Term (up to 12 months) Level 8 - $117,936 to $133,494 p.a. (plus 17% superannuation) Hybrid and remote work options supported Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Port Macquarie, Wagga Wagga or Remote As a Workplace Relations Specialist, you will be a key advisor on complex employee and industrial relations matters across Charles Sturt University. Reporting to the Director, Workplace Relations and Compliance, you will provide expert guidance on workplace legislation, industrial instruments, dispute resolution, misconduct and performance matters, and enterprise bargaining activities. You will partner closely with leaders across the University to mitigate risk, build capability and support positive workplace outcomes. This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced ER/IR professional seeking exposure to complex, high-impact work within a large and geographically dispersed organisation. About you To succeed in this role, you will be a trusted advisor who can confidently navigate complex workplace matters while building productive relationships across a diverse stakeholder group. You will bring: Relevant tertiary qualifications in employment relations, industrial relations, human resources, law or a related discipline. Significant experience in employee and industrial relations within a large or complex organisational environment. Strong knowledge of employment law, industrial relations frameworks and enterprise agreement development and implementation. Demonstrated experience managing complex workplace matters with sound judgement, discretion and confidentiality. Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder engagement skills, including policy development and advisory experience. Strong analytical, problem-solving and relationship-building capabilities. About us We are a University of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Division of People and Culture here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, and address the selection criteria in the position description and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Recruitment specific enquiries: Rebecca Dwyer | Acting Manager, Talent Acquisition | redwyer@csu.edu.au Job specific enquiries: Bronte Buesnell | Workplace Relations Specialist | bbuesnell@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, Monday 23 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 7bf6b5b1 Last Name (required) d8be29ab Email (required) 1e29f490 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Project Manager, Graduate Research Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Orange, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Project Management Lead strategic projects and initiatives that enhance the higher degree research experience, training and graduate research outcomes. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4c42f0aa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Fixed Term - Full Time Fixed Term - Full Time Locations Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Other, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Other, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) d8520693 Last Name (required) e12b7e53 Email (required) bec70e5b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
