    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/administrative-assistant-albury-wodonga-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant - Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Fixed Term - Part Time Closing on: Nov 19 2026 Position Description Join a supportive team in a nurturing early learning environment Make a difference supporting children, families and educators Enjoy a varied administrative role with opportunities to grow The role Part time, Fixed term up to 6 months (24 hours a week) Level 4 - $51,971 to $56,416 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Albury Wodonga We are seeking a highly organised and proactive Administrative Assistant to join our Children's Centre team. In this role, you will provide a range of clerical and administrative support to the Director, Assistant Director and Centre staff, helping ensure the smooth and efficient day-to-day operation of the service. As a key first point of contact, you will play an important role in creating a welcoming and positive experience for families, carers and prospective clients. Your responsibilities will include maintaining accurate electronic and manual records, managing attendance and payment information, processing accounts and purchase orders, assisting with government reporting requirements and facilitating communication with families. You will also support the ongoing administrative and compliance requirements of the Centre, contributing to a collaborative team environment that is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and high-quality early learning experience. About you Demonstrated administrative and clerical experience, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and maintain accurate records. Strong computer skills, including proficiency in Microsoft Office applications such as Word, Excel and Outlook, and the ability to learn and use various software systems. Well-developed communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build positive relationships and provide friendly, responsive service to families, staff and the wider community. A proactive and flexible approach, with the ability to use initiative, exercise sound judgement and work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. A genuine commitment to supporting children and families, with an understanding of the importance of providing a safe, welcoming and inclusive childcare environment. Desirable (not essential): A Certificate III in Early Childhood Education and Care, or some knowledge or experience within the early childhood education and care sector, would be advantageous. As part of this recruitment, a pre-employment functional screening is required. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Early Learning and Nurture Centre here. Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a cover letter that tells us more about you and upload your CV. This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Job specific enquiries: Monica Graham | Director, Children's Centre | mograham@csu.edu.au Please note we will be reviewing applications on submission. The position may be filled before the closing date, we encourage you to apply at your earliest convenience. Applications will close once the role is filled, or by 11pm 19 November 2026, whichever comes first. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0be3edef Last Name (required) d0b063e2 Email (required) 48ec3c66 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Project Manager, Graduate Research Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Orange, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Project Management Lead strategic projects and initiatives that enhance the higher degree research experience, training and graduate research outcomes. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f24b5892 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Child Care Administration Child Care Employment Type Fixed Term - Part Time Fixed Term - Part Time Locations Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 7c96ddc8 Last Name (required) 26397c22 Email (required) f4579de6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
