    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/agripark-casual-employment-register-wagga-wagga-nsw-australia-d746a56b-1086-4477-8fc1-86c119af5978": {
      "title": "AgriPark Casual Employment Register",
      "description": "AgriPark Casual Employment Register - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode AgriPark Casual Employment Register Wagga Wagga, NSW Casual Closing on: May 2 2027 What is the AgriPark Casual Employment Register? The AgriPark Casual Employment Register allows individuals to express interest in casual agricultural and farm‑based work at the University. When short‑term or seasonal work opportunities arise within AgriPark, the University reviews this register and may contact suitably skilled candidates to discuss potential casual engagements. Being on the register does not guarantee employment; however, it enables us to quickly connect with people who have relevant skills and availability when needs arise. Who should apply? We welcome expression of interest from individuals with relevant skills and experience in one or more of the following areas; General farm labour Livestock handling and animal care Biosecurity Soil sampling Cropping operations Horticulture and/ or vineyard work Research field technical officers Cellar door staff with RSA How Does It Work? 1. Express Your Interest Complete the online application form and provide details about your: Skills and experience Availability Preferred location (if applicable) Pay rate expectations 2. Stay on the Register Your application will remain active on the register for up to six (6) months. You may update or withdraw your application at any time if your circumstances change. 3. Potential Opportunities If a casual or temporary opportunity becomes available that matches your skills and availability, you may be contacted to discuss the role. 4. Employment Conditions Casual employees are engaged by the university in accordance with applicable industrial and statutory requirements. How to Apply If you are interested in joining the AgriPark Casual Employment Register , please apply online and complete the application form. For further information, please contact jobs@csu.edu.au Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a1a45651 Last Name (required) 30bd687c Email (required) 2fae3066 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d7757f61 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Sustainability Sustainability Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 5e40a59e Last Name (required) b797efea Email (required) 4b3c24ae Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles St