    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/lecturers-identified-first-nations-position-albury-wodonga-nsw-australia-bathurst-dubbo-orange-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Lecturers - Identified First Nations Position",
      "description": "Lecturers - Identified First Nations Position - Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Dubbo, NSW, Australia - Orange, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Lecturers - Identified First Nations Position Albury-Wodonga, NSW Bathurst, NSW Dubbo, NSW Orange, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Show More Show Less Continuing - Full Time Closing on: Nov 19 2026 Position Description Grow your career and connect with mob at the university where you belong​ The role Multiple positions available Level B - $ to $117,825 to $134,965 p.a. (plus 17% superannuation) Albury-Wodonga, Bathurst, Dubbo, Orange, Port Macquarie or Wagga Wagga The opportunity Are you nearing completion of your PhD, recently awarded your doctorate, or an established academic looking for your next opportunity? Charles Sturt University is seeking Expressions of Interest from passionate and talented researchers interested in pursuing a Lecturer (Level B) Teaching and Research career across a broad range of disciplines and Schools throughout the University. We are building a talent pool of exceptional academics who are committed to delivering outstanding student experiences while contributing to impactful research that makes a difference to regional communities and beyond. As a Lecturer (Teaching and Research), you will contribute to the University's mission through a balanced academic workload that includes: Delivering engaging, student-centred teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programs Designing and enhancing contemporary curriculum and learning experiences Conducting high-quality research and scholarly activity within your discipline Publishing research outcomes and participating in collaborative research initiatives Building partnerships with industry, community and professional stakeholders Contributing to academic leadership, service and the broader University community We are interested in hearing from candidates across all academic disciplines and Schools, including emerging and established researchers whose expertise aligns with our teaching and research priorities. About us At Charles Sturt University, we deeply value the knowledges, cultures and leadership that First Nations peoples bring. We're committed to building a culturally safe and inclusive workplace where mob feel respected, supported and connected. We're growing our First Nations workforce, with opportunities across teaching, research, student support and other professional roles. Bring your skills, experience and perspectives to meaningful work that supports our students, communities and future generations.​ When you join Charles Sturt, you'll be part of a connected First Nations staff community, with opportunities for professional development, cultural leave and connection through First Nations Staff Connect. We're committed to supporting First Nations careers and creating a workplace where mob feel valued, connected and supported to succeed.​ Learn more about Charles Sturt University here . Visit our website to learn about First Nations careers at Charles Sturt . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. This is an identified Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander position under section 14 of the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act, 1977. Please be aware you may be asked to provide confirmation of Indigenous Australian Identity. To apply If you are interested in exploring future Lecturer (Teaching and Research) opportunities at Charles Sturt University, we encourage you to submit a statement outlining: Your discipline area(s) of expertise Research interests and achievements Teaching experience Preferred campus location(s) To apply, click Apply and complete the online application form, upload your CV and a brief statement (max 1-2 pages) outlining your suitability and interests above. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . We welcome expressions of interest from candidates across all disciplines and Schools. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Office of the Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Academic) | provost@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 19 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d71a0664 Last Name (required) 5ea32a7f Email (required) f781695c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c9dd2335 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Indigenous Identified Indigenous Identified Employment Type Continuing - Full Time Continuing - Full Time Locations Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) df90c816 Last Name (required) 154b0f5e Email (required) 73236ad2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
