    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/chief-financial-officer-albury-wodonga-nsw-australia-bathurst-dubbo-orange-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "Chief Financial Officer - Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Dubbo, NSW, Australia - Orange, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Chief Financial Officer Albury-Wodonga, NSW Bathurst, NSW Dubbo, NSW Orange, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Show More Show Less Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 16 2026 Position Description We are a university deeply connected to the land, people and communities of regional Australia. We develop capable, forward-thinking graduates and professionals who create meaningful impact, helping their communities thrive today and into the future. Through strong regional foundations and enduring partnerships, we build connections that extend across Australia and resonate globally. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means \"the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in\". It lies at the heart of Charles Sturt University and shapes our values, culture and purpose. Grounded in traditional Indigenous knowledge, it also reflects the enduring role of universities: to create, share and apply knowledge that improves lives and contributes to a better future. As a distributed yet connected university, we harness technology and innovation to bring people together across locations, communities and disciplines. Our ambition is to be Australia's leading regional university, renowned for research excellence and for delivering regional outcomes with global impact. Reporting to the Chief Operating Officer, The Chief Financial Officer (CFO) is a key executive leadership role responsible for shaping the University's long-term financial sustainability, revenue strategy and broader institutional direction. The CFO will lead a significant program of finance transformation and process improvement, driving contemporary financial practices, system enhancements and operational efficiencies across a complex and geographically dispersed organisation. The CFO will provide high-quality financial analysis, advice and strategic options to support University-wide decision-making. The role will engage confidently with key internal and external stakeholders, while also supporting the Vice-Chancellor, Executive Leadership Team and the University Council on finance-related matters and presentations. The successful candidate will bring a proven track record of leading finance-system transformation and delivering genuine operational efficiencies. They will combine strong financial and commercial acumen with the ability to act as an effective enterprise business partner. Experience working across complex, multi-site or geographically dispersed organisations will be important, as will the ability to lead, engage and develop a distributed finance team. Experience in Higher education  would be  highly regarded, however outstanding candidates from relevant public-sector, service-intensive or other similar / adjacent complex environments will also be considered. The successful candidate will demonstrate sound judgement, clear communication, collaborative leadership and the credibility to influence across an institution. Equally comfortable operating at both strategic and operational levels,  they will play a critical role in supporting Charles Sturt University's continued financial strength, sustainability and evolution as a student-centred institution with a strong regional mission and global outlook. Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To learn more about this unique opportunity please contact our advising consultants Alun Parry, Andrew Ng and Dr Margot Courtillat at Boyden on +61 2 9225 7400, or margot.courtillat@boyden.com Applications close on 16 November 2026 Back to job search Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 1305339b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Executive Finance Executive Finance Employment Type Fixed Term - Full Time Fixed Term - Full Time Locations Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 081ee474 Last Name (required) 80651548 Email (required) 994e4530 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/adviser-first-nations-students-identified-first-nations-position-port-macquarie-nsw-australia-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Adviser, First Nations Students - Identified First Nations Position",
      "description": "Adviser, First Nations Students - Identified First Nations Position - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Adviser, First Nations Students - Identified First Nations Position Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Continuing - Full Time Closing on: Nov 19 2026 Position Description Grow your career and connect with mob at the university where you belong​ The role Full Time, Continuing Level 6 - $95,246 to $103,022 p.a. (plus 17% superannuation) Port Macquarie and Wagga Wagga Are you passionate about supporting First Nations students to thrive at university and achieve their goals? As an Adviser, First Nations Students, you will play a vital role in creating a positive and culturally safe student experience. Working as part of the First Nations Student Connect team, you'll provide personalised advice, advocacy and support to students throughout their university journey, helping them navigate challenges, access services, build connections, and succeed academically and personally. You'll engage with students individually and through group programs, both on campus and online, building trusted relationships that foster belonging, confidence and success. You'll also collaborate closely with colleagues across the University, as well as families, communities and external organisations, to ensure students receive coordinated and culturally responsive support. This is a rewarding opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of First Nations students while contributing to the University's commitment to student success, equity and inclusion. About you To be successful in this role, you will bring: Experience supporting First Nations peoples using culturally responsive, strengths-based and inclusive approaches. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships and work effectively with students, communities, colleagues and external stakeholders. Well-developed organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, exercise initiative and deliver high-quality outcomes. A collaborative and student-centred approach, with a genuine commitment to supporting student success and wellbeing. Confidence using technology and learning new systems to deliver efficient and effective services. Appointment will be conditional upon the successful applicant satisfying and maintaining a “Working with Children Check”, in accordance with the Commission for Children and Young People Act (NSW). About us At Charles Sturt University, we deeply value the knowledges, cultures and leadership that First Nations peoples bring. We're committed to building a culturally safe and inclusive workplace where mob feel respected, supported and connected. We're growing our First Nations workforce, with opportunities across teaching, research, student support and other professional roles. Bring your skills, experience and perspectives to meaningful work that supports our students, communities and future generations.​ When you join Charles Sturt, you'll be part of a connected First Nations staff community, with opportunities for professional development, cultural leave and connection through First Nations Staff Connect. We're committed to supporting First Nations careers and creating a workplace where mob feel valued, connected and supported to succeed.​ Learn more about the Division of Student Success here . Visit our website to learn about First Nations careers at Charles Sturt . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. This is an identified Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander position under section 14 of the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act, 1977. Please be aware you may be asked to provide confirmation of Indigenous Australian Identity. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Blake Dunn | Senior Manager, First Nations Student Services | bdunn@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 19 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 7de5c4c7 Last Name (required) 8e432fcc Email (required) b56f7e63 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4ba5d8a6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Indigenous Identified Indigenous Identified Employment Type Continuing - Full Time Continuing - Full Time Locations Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 92813ea2 Last Name (required) ae542347 Email (required) 9ff9bd41 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
