    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/associate-lecturer-lecturer-in-enabling-education-bathurst-nsw-australia-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer / Lecturer in Enabling Education",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer / Lecturer in Enabling Education - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Associate Lecturer / Lecturer in Enabling Education Bathurst, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Continuing - Part Time Closing on: Nov 11 2026 Position Description Engage with best practice in the Fee Free Uni Ready environment Teach in an innovative, collegiate team Regionally located role with requirement for on campus teaching The role Part Time – 22.5 hours per week, Continuing Preferred days of work - Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday Level A - $48,027 to $64,922 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Level B - $68,304 to $80,979 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Bathurst, Port Macquarie or Wagga Wagga At Charles Sturt University, we believe everyone deserves the opportunity to succeed in higher education. Our Enabling and Transition team deliver open access, capacity building subjects which provide diverse students with basis for entry to degree courses. The role is regionally based, and the incumbent will be required to be available to teach face-to-face on the Charles Sturt campus where they are located. The successful applicant will be a passionate and experienced educator with deep understanding of inclusive practice and enabling pedagogies as well as discipline expertise in one or more of the following: academic literacies, mathematics, science and/or TESOL. The role demands high levels of competence with digital technologies and demonstrated experience and/or preparedness to develop skills in curriculum design. This is an opportunity to join a student-centred team committed to best practice in widening participation. You will play a key role in changing higher education outcomes in rural and regional Australia and have impact on an identified strategic growth area in the University. About you A relevant doctoral qualification (Level B) or postgraduate qualification (Level A) or equivalent accreditation and standing. Demonstrated expertise in teaching with impact in one or more of the following: academic literacies, mathematics, science and/or TESOL. Demonstrated competence in current digital teaching technologies and practices with preparedness to innovate and commitment to quality and standards. Experience with working collaboratively and independently in an academic setting. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Division of Student Success here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description(s) below: Position Description - Level A - Associate Lecturer in Enabling Education Position Description - Level B - Lecturer in Enabling Education or by contacting: General Enquiries: jobs@csu.edu.au Job specific enquiries: Dr Carolyn O’Dwyer | Program Director (Enabling and Transition) | codwyer@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 11 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 4880b020 Last Name (required) 9f273b56 Email (required) a8c921f0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 7fb3348b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic - Teaching Focussed Academic - Teaching Focussed Employment Type Continuing - Part Time Continuing - Part Time Locations Bathurst, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 3ea884dc Last Name (required) 69600bbc Email (required) 646dcc8c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
