    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/digital-learning-officer-bathurst-nsw-australia-orange-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Digital Learning Officer",
      "description": "Digital Learning Officer - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Orange, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Digital Learning Officer Bathurst, NSW Orange, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 12 2026 Position Description Create engaging online learning content Support academics using Brightspace and digital tools Combine creativity and technology to enhance student success. The role Full Time, Fixed Term (12 months) Level 6 - $95,246 to $103,022 p.a. (plus 17% superannuation) Bathurst, Orange or Wagga Wagga At Charles Sturt University, we're committed to delivering exceptional learning experiences for our students. As a Digital Learning Officer, you'll combine creativity, technology, and innovation to develop high-quality digital learning resources that enhance teaching, learning, and assessment across the university. You will partner with academic staff to develop high-quality digital learning experiences using the University’s Brightspace learning management system and a range of educational technologies. Working at the intersection of technology and teaching practice, you will help translate teaching intent into engaging, accessible, and effective online learning activities and resources. We are particularly interested in candidates with skills in audio-visual production, animation, or advanced interactive content development who can bring creative and technical expertise to the team. In this role, you will develop bespoke digital learning resources, build academic capability through practical guidance, and support innovative approaches to digital content development, including the appropriate use of emerging AI technologies. You will apply accessibility, copyright, brand, and quality standards, while managing competing priorities and delivering work to agreed timelines. You will also contribute to improving digital development practices and building relevant capability across the University. About you You enjoy working with people, solving problems, and creating digital content that makes a difference. You will bring: Experience developing high-quality digital content within an educational, training or learning environment. Knowledge of educational technology and online platforms The ability to manage tasks and meet deadlines Confidence supporting and training staff A strong focus on quality, accessibility, and clear design A collaborative mindset with a passion for innovation and continuous improvement. Experience in higher education (desirable, not essential) About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Division of Learning and Teaching here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” (maximum 1 page) demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Recruitment specific enquiries: Nelvin Kumar | Talent Acquisition Consultant | nekumar@csu.edu.au Job specific enquiries: Ryun Fell | Manager, Educational Technologies | rfell@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 12 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a277d9d6 Last Name (required) 89135f71 Email (required) fba3617e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a845e48b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education and Training or Learning Support (i.e. Academic Skills, Educational Designers) Professional Education and Training or Learning Support (i.e. Academic Skills, Educational Designers) Professional Employment Type Fixed Term - Full Time Fixed Term - Full Time Locations Bathurst, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 40ce39aa Last Name (required) 79605fd7 Email (required) 071b7de4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept