    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-functional-biomaterials-for-sustainable-agriculture-wagga-wagga-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - Functional Biomaterials for Sustainable Agriculture",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - Functional Biomaterials for Sustainable Agriculture - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Research Fellow - Functional Biomaterials for Sustainable Agriculture Wagga Wagga, NSW Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 10 2026 Position Description Drive research that turns agricultural waste into sustainable solutions Work with industry on innovative biomaterials and agricultural products Make an impact across research, sustainability and commercialisation The role Full Time, Fixed Term (up to 12 months) Level A - $80,046 to $108,204 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Wagga Wagga As a Postdoctoral Research Fellow, you will support an ARC Mid-Career Industry Fellowship project focused on transforming agricultural waste into low-cost, high-quality substrates and soil amendment products. You will develop controlled-release biomaterials designed to improve nutrient release and water retention for mushroom cultivation and crop growth. Working with industry partners and a multidisciplinary research team, you will plan and deliver experimental research spanning nanomaterials synthesis and characterisation, laboratory studies, plant and soil experiments, data analysis and research translation. You will contribute to publications, reports and project milestones while supporting the scale-up, commercialisation and practical application of research outcomes. About you A PhD in materials science, chemistry, chemical engineering, nanotechnology, agricultural science, agronomy, soil science or a related discipline. Research experience in areas such as agricultural-waste valorisation, mushroom cultivation, substrate development, nutrient-release studies or plant and soil experiments. Demonstrated ability to design rigorous experiments, analyse quantitative data and maintain reproducible research records. A strong record of research outputs, with high-level scientific writing, presentation and collaboration skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively, manage competing priorities and build productive relationships with researchers and industry partners. You will bring curiosity, innovation and a collaborative approach to applied research, with the ability to translate scientific ideas into practical outcomes. Experience in nanomaterials, scale-up, industry validation, commercialisation or analytical techniques such as microscopy, spectroscopy or nutrient-release assays will be highly regarded. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Gulbali Institute here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, and address the selection criteria in the position description and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Job specific enquiries: Li Li | Principal Research Fellow of Advanced Biomineral Nanomaterials | lili@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 10 November 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 1e456f01 Last Name (required) 2f2072b2 Email (required) 4ab8d61c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c71385c7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic - Research Only/Fellowship Academic - Research Only/Fellowship Employment Type Fixed Term - Full Time Fixed Term - Full Time Locations Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 5ee66326 Last Name (required) e9a3a2b4 Email (required) a7da1e6e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
