    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/head-school-of-computing-mathematics-and-engineering-bathurst-nsw-australia-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Head, School of Computing, Mathematics and Engineering",
      "description": "Head, School of Computing, Mathematics and Engineering - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Head, School of Computing, Mathematics and Engineering Bathurst, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Dec 7 2026 Position Description Shape the future of STEM education, research and innovation. Lead a high-performing school with national influence and impact. Join Australia's leading regional university and inspire excellence. The role Full Time, Fixed Term (up to 5 years) Senior Leader, Level 4 Remuneration package starting from $208,921 pa (including superannuation) Bathurst, Port Macquarie or Wagga Wagga You are a contemporary academic leader with a strong track record of delivering results in complex higher education environments. Combining strategic vision with operational excellence, you have successfully led people, resources and change while creating a culture of accountability, collaboration and continuous improvement. You bring a doctoral qualification in a discipline relevant to computing, information technology, mathematics or engineering, together with significant leadership experience in a multidisciplinary university environment. You have demonstrated success in improving teaching quality and student outcomes, building research capability and impact, managing significant budgets and resources, and developing high-performing teams. Equally comfortable engaging with academics, students, industry, government and professional bodies, you are recognised for your ability to build strong partnerships, influence outcomes and inspire others around a shared vision. Most importantly, you are committed to creating an inclusive and supportive environment that reflects the values of Charles Sturt University and supports excellence in learning, research and engagement. About you You are an accomplished academic leader with a track record of delivering excellence in teaching, research and engagement. You combine strategic thinking with strong people leadership and are passionate about creating positive outcomes for students, staff and industry. You will bring: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline Significant leadership experience in higher education or a comparable environment A proven ability to lead and develop high-performing teams Experience driving excellence in learning, teaching and research Strong financial, operational and resource management capabilities Exceptional stakeholder engagement and partnership-building skills The ability to lead change, influence outcomes and deliver strategic results A commitment to fostering an inclusive, collaborative and high-performing culture. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the School of Computing, Mathematics and Engineering here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, and address the selection criteria in the position description and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the Applicant Information Brochure or by contacting: Recruitment specific enquiries: Rebecca Dwyer | Manager, Talent Acquisition | redwyer@csu.edu.au Job specific enquiries: Professor Lewis Bizo | Executive Dean, Faculty of Business, Justice and Behavioural Sciences | lbizo@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 7 December 2026 Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d492c589 Last Name (required) 1254c7e3 Email (required) c8225ba0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 16c5ab6b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic - Leadership Executive Academic - Leadership Executive Employment Type Fixed Term - Full Time Fixed Term - Full Time Locations Bathurst, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) e14c6fb6 Last Name (required) 5528328c Email (required) 11790bd0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential onl