    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/casual-employment-register-albury-wodonga-nsw-australia-bathurst-dubbo-orange-port-macquarie-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Casual Employment Register",
      "description": "Casual Employment Register - Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Dubbo, NSW, Australia - Orange, NSW, Australia - Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Casual Employment Register Albury-Wodonga, NSW Bathurst, NSW Dubbo, NSW Orange, NSW Port Macquarie, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Show More Show Less Casual Closing on: Dec 31 2026 Are you looking for casual work opportunities? Charles Sturt University maintains a Casual Employment Register for individuals interested in casual or short-term employment opportunities across various general and professional functions. What is the Casual Employment Register? Our Casual Employment Register is for people interested in working at the university on a casual basis in non-academic roles. When temporary needs arise, we review the register and contact suitable candidates to discuss potential assignments. Please note if you are looking for casual academic work visit our casual academic register . Who Should Apply? We welcome expressions of interest from individuals with relevant skills and experience in areas such as: Administration Child Care Customer service Facilities and Maintenance Finance Hospitality Information Technology Learning and Teaching Support Library Marketing & Communications Research Radio Technical and specialist higher education support roles How Does It Work? Express Your Interest – Complete the online application form, including information about your skills, experience, availability, preferred location, and pay rate expectations. Stay on the Register – Your details will remain on our register for up to three months. If your circumstances change, you can update or remove your information. Potential Opportunities – When a casual/temporary role becomes available that matches your skills and availability, we may contact you to discuss the opportunity. Employment Conditions – Casual employees are engaged by the university in accordance with applicable industrial and statutory requirements. Benefits of joining Flexibility – Pick up work that suits your schedule. Experience – Gain valuable experience in different roles and departments. Potential for continuing roles – While there are no guarantees, casual roles can sometimes lead to longer-term employment opportunities for those who are interested in permanent roles. How to Apply If you’re interested in joining our Casual Employment Register , please apply now and complete an application. For further information, contact jobs@csu.edu.au . We look forward to hearing from you! Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) c1d883bd Last Name (required) e29f4d77 Email (required) 55a4ca40 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. Workplace Relations Specialist Albury-Wodonga, NSW. Bathurst, NSW. Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Other, NSW. Port Macquarie, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Human Resources Shape the future of employee relations, drive positive change, lead strategic initiatives, and ensure compliance in a high-impact university role. Administrative Assistant Albury-Wodonga, NSW Administration, Child Care Provide essential administrative support in a welcoming childcare environment, helping deliver quality services to children and families. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 83759c48 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Building and Property Services Catering Services Child Care Customer Service Data Analysis Dentistry Finance Health Services Human Resources Administration Building and Property Services Catering Services Child Care Customer Service Data Analysis Dentistry Finance Health Services Human Resources Employment Type Casual Casual Locations Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Albury-Wodonga, NSW, Australia Bathurst, NSW, Australia Dubbo, NSW, Australia Orange, NSW, Australia Port Macquarie, NSW, Australia Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia First Name (required) 04fe5336 Last Name (required) 2da854e2 Email (required) c436f74a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
