    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/recruitment-administrator-bathurst-nsw-australia-wagga-wagga": {
      "title": "Recruitment Administrator",
      "description": "Recruitment Administrator - Bathurst, NSW, Australia - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Recruitment Administrator Bathurst, NSW Wagga Wagga, NSW Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 22 2026 Position Description Fixed term role to June 2027 supporting a major recruitment program High volume interview and employment contract coordination Use your Excel, Outlook and administration expertise The role Full Time, Fixed Term (until June 2027) Level 5 - $84,869 to $92,654 p.a. (plus 17% superannuation) Bathurst or Wagga Wagga Are you highly organised, process-driven and thrive in a fast-paced environment where attention to detail matters? Charles Sturt University is seeking a Recruitment Administrator to support a significant internal recruitment program. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys coordinating complex schedules, managing high volumes of work, and ensuring every detail is completed accurately and on time. Working within the Talent Acquisition team, you will provide critical administrative and coordination support across a large volume of recruitment activity. You will play a key role in ensuring recruitment processes run smoothly and candidates, hiring managers and stakeholders receive a seamless experience. Key responsibilities include: Coordinating high volumes of interviews across multiple calendars using Microsoft Outlook and Teams Managing complex scheduling requirements involving candidates, hiring managers and panel members Preparing, processing and issuing employment contracts and recruitment documentation Maintaining accurate candidate and recruitment records Managing recruitment workflows and communications within recruitment systems Producing and updating spreadsheets to track recruitment activity and reporting Responding to enquiries and providing administrative support to stakeholders throughout the recruitment process Following established processes and procedures to ensure accuracy, compliance and consistency About you You are someone who enjoys structure, organisation and delivering high-quality work at pace. You can comfortably manage repetitive administrative tasks while maintaining exceptional attention to detail. To be successful, you will bring: Demonstrated experience recruitment coordination or a similar high-volume support role Advanced Microsoft Outlook calendar management and scheduling capabilities Strong Microsoft Excel skills and confidence working with spreadsheets and data Exceptional organisational and time management skills Experience processing large volumes of documentation accurately and efficiently A strong customer service mindset and ability to build positive stakeholder relationships Excellent written and verbal communication skills The ability to prioritise competing demands while maintaining accuracy and confidentiality Experience using HR, recruitment or applicant tracking systems will be highly regarded About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Division of People and Culture here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Rebecca Dwyer | Manager, Talent Acquisition | redwyer@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 22 November 2026 Recommended Jobs Project Manager, Extension & Adoption Dubbo, NSW. Orange, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional, Project Management Turn agricultural research into real-world impact by leading extension projects and driving innovation and adoption across the industry. Director, Centre for Law and Justice Canberra, ACT. Bathurst, NSW Academic - Leadership Lead the strategic direction of a dynamic Centre driving excellence in law, justice, research and engagement. APPN Node Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead a multidisciplinary team, drive major research projects and grow Australia's plant phenotyping capabilities. 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
