    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-other-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow - Other, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Research Fellow Other, NSW Fixed Term - Full Time Closing on: Nov 25 2026 Position Description Contribute to impactful research in a globally significant river system Collaborate with leading freshwater ecologists and industry partners Build your research profile through an exciting One Basin CRC project The role Full Time, Fixed Term (up to August 2029) Level A/B - $80,046 to $134,965 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Must be based in a OneBasin regional hub (Griffith, Loxton, Mildura, Goondiwindi) Join Charles Sturt University's Gulbali Institute for Agriculture, Water and Environment as a Postdoctoral Research Fellow, contributing to the One Basin CRC research project, Confluences: Integrated Data for Fish and River Health Across the Murray–Darling Basin. This exciting project aims to address fragmented environmental datasets across the Basin, improving how information is accessed, integrated and used to support river restoration and citizen science initiatives. You will play a key role in identifying and securing access to diverse datasets, developing robust and scalable data pipelines, and establishing validation workflows to support an open-source data warehouse that informs whole-of-Basin decision-making. Working alongside a world-class team of freshwater ecologists, you will build relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders, including researchers, government representatives, First Nations communities, data engineers and recreational fishing groups. You will collaborate with end-users to translate complex research data into accessible, practical outputs, while contributing to high-quality research, publications and presentations. This is an excellent opportunity to develop your research portfolio while making a meaningful contribution to the health and resilience of freshwater ecosystems across the Murray–Darling Basin. About you A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline, or equivalent accreditation and standing. Highly developed analytical, critical thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to embrace emerging technologies and apply innovative solutions. Demonstrated experience building effective partnerships and collaborative relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to produce and present high-quality research and technical information to varied audiences. A commitment to culturally respectful, inclusive and safe workplace practices, together with a current Australian driver's licence. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Gulbali Institute here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, and address the selection criteria in the position description and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Job specific enquiries: Rupert Mathwin | Research Fellow in Freshwater Ecology | rmathwin@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 25 November 2026 Recommended Jobs Dental Receptionist Dubbo, NSW Administration, Dentistry Be the welcoming face of our Dubbo Dental and Oral Health Clinic, supporting patients and keeping appointments running smoothly. Lecturer in Psychology Bathurst, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Academic - Teaching and Research Help shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and community impact. Lecturer in Engineering Bathurst, NSW Academic - Teaching Focussed Make a lasting impact in engineering education through teaching excellence, innovation and student success. 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/team-leader-front-desk-wagga-wagga-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Team Leader, Front Desk",
      "description": "Team Leader, Front Desk - Wagga Wagga, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Team Leader, Front Desk Wagga Wagga, NSW Continuing - Full Time Closing on: Nov 26 2026 Position Description Lead and develop a reception team supporting dental care and student learning Shape a welcoming patient experience and improve day-to-day clinic operations Enjoy a varied, hands-on leadership role with great staff benefits The role Full Time, Continuing - 35 hours per week Level 5 - $84,869 to $92,654 pa (plus 17% superannuation) On-site, Wagga Wagga Dental and Oral Health Clinic based role Lead our reception team to create a welcoming patient experience across the Dental and Oral Health Clinics. Work closely with clinicians and students to support quality dental care and student learning. Develop staff, coordinate rosters and oversee appointments, patient accounts and billing, while providing hands-on reception support when needed. Help shape better ways of working, resolve patient concerns and guide staff in using the patient management system, keeping patient records accurate and confidential. About you Relevant qualifications, skills and/or experience in reception, administration or customer service. Experience in clinical reception or administration, including leading and developing a team through change. Strong organisational and financial skills to manage priorities, patient accounts and reconciliations. Knowledge of patient management and appointment systems, with the ability to train others. Effective communication, problem-solving and complaint resolution skills, with accuracy and commitment to privacy and compliance. About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the Dental and Oral Health Clinic here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, submit a “statement of suitability” demonstrating your skills, knowledge and/or experience relevant to the position (referencing the selection criteria in the position description) and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process, please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Job specific enquiries: Kate Giles | Business Manager | BusinessManager-DOHC@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 26 November 2026 Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer in Clinical Psychology and Course Director Bathurst, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Academic - Leadership, Academic - Teaching Focussed, Health Services Deliver impactful learning, teaching and course design - contributing to developing future Psychologists for regional, rural and remote Australia. Dental Receptionist Dubbo, NSW Administration, Dentistry Be the welcoming face of our Dubbo Dental and Oral Health Clinic, supporting patients and keeping appointments running smoothly. Lecturer in Psychology Bathurst, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Academic - Teaching and Research Help shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and community impact. 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
