    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/jobs/psychology-clinic-director-bathurst-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Psychology Clinic Director",
      "description": "Psychology Clinic Director - Bathurst, NSW, Australia Visit Charles Sturt University Existing Applicant? Sign up for jobs alerts My Profile Kiosk mode Psychology Clinic Director Bathurst, NSW Fixed Term - Part Time Closing on: Nov 29 2026 Position Description Lead a psychology clinic shaping the next generation of psychologists Deliver meaningful community impact through accessible mental health services Join a collaborative team shaping the future of Psychology education The role Part Time (0.8 FTE), Fixed Term (until June 2027) Remuneration package in the range of $147,808 - $168,274 pa (including allowance and 17% superannuation) Bathurst As the Clinic Director, you will provide strategic leadership and professional oversight of the Charles Sturt Psychology Clinic, ensuring the delivery of high-quality psychological services while supporting the education and development of future psychologists. This is a unique opportunity to shape clinical training, strengthen community partnerships, drive service innovation, and ensure the highest standards of governance, ethics and client care. Working closely with academic staff, students, industry partners and community stakeholders, you will play a pivotal role in advancing both community mental health outcomes and the University's strategic vision. About you Registration as a Clinical Psychologist and Psychology Board of Australia approved supervisor status Extensive experience delivering evidence-based psychological services, ideally within a clinical or health setting Proven leadership capability, with experience managing, coordinating or developing clinical services, training programs or multidisciplinary teams Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to build productive partnerships across universities, industry, government and community sectors A commitment to excellence in clinical governance, student development, quality improvement, innovation and culturally responsive practice About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles Sturt University – our ethos. It comes from traditional Indigenous Australian knowledge, but it also speaks to the mission of universities – to develop and spread wisdom to make the world a better place. Harnessing technology, we thrive as a distributed yet connected community, welcoming and engaging with people across Australia and the world. Learn more about the School of Psychology here . Visit our website to learn about our great range of employee benefits . Charles Sturt University is committed to building a diverse workforce as shown through our Athena Swan Bronze Award, our Australian Workplace Equality Index Bronze Award and our membership of a range of diversity focused organisations including Diversity Council Australia and Pride in Diversity. We encourage applications from First Nations people, carers, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, neurodivergent people, and people of all age groups, genders and sexualities for all roles. To apply Click the Apply button and complete your application online, and address the selection criteria in the position description and upload your CV. If you experience difficulties applying online or for further information on completing the application process please visit our how to apply page or contact us . This position is open to Australian Citizens and Permanent Residents; or applicants who hold a current valid work visa commensurate with this position. Disclosure Requirement Applicants may be required to disclose information relating to gender-based violence allegations or findings as part of the University's recruitment and screening processes. Further information Additional information is available in the position description or by contacting: Associate Professor Robyn Brunton | Head, School of Psychology | HOS-SOP@csu.edu.au Closing Date: 11pm, 29 November 2026 Back to job search Recommended Jobs Grazing and Livestock Manager Wagga Wagga, NSW Management, Professional Lead grazing and livestock operations at Charles Sturt University, driving best practice, innovation and sustainable farm management. Team Leader, Front Desk Wagga Wagga, NSW Administration, Professional Build your leadership career at Charles Sturt University and support dental care for the Wagga Wagga community in a full-time, continuing role. Senior Lecturer in Clinical Psychology and Course Director Bathurst, NSW. Wagga Wagga, NSW Academic - Leadership, Academic - Teaching Focussed, Health Services Deliver impactful learning, teaching and course design - contributing to developing future Psychologists for regional, rural and remote Australia. 'Yindyamarra winhanganha' The wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in We pay our respect to all First Nations elders both past and present from the lands where Charles Sturt University students reside. In particular, we acknowledge the Wiradjuri, Ngunawal, Gundungurra and Birpai peoples of Australia, who are the traditional custodians of the land where Charles Sturt University campuses are located. Stay connected Facebook X Youtube Instagram LinkedIn © 2026 Charles Sturt University - TEQSA Provider Identification: PRV12018 (Australian University). CRICOS Provider: 00005F. Accessibility Privacy Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential o